# Atomic Design — no `className` prop

## Rule

- Do **not** expose or pass `className` to components in `atoms`, `molecules`, or `organisms`.
- Do **not** pass `className` from `templates` or `components` into atomic components.
- Style atomic components with **boolean props** that map to predefined Tailwind classes (e.g. `mt4` → `mt-4`, `gap4` → `gap-4`).
- If a new style is needed, add a boolean (or enum) prop on the atom/molecule and implement the class map inside that layer.

## Spacing scale

Use numeric suffix = Tailwind spacing token:

| Prop   | Class  |
|--------|--------|
| `mt1`  | `mt-1` |
| `mt4`  | `mt-4` |
| `gap4` | `gap-4` |
| `px4`  | `px-4` |

Shared builders live in `src/ui/atoms/shared/spacingClasses.ts`.

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅
<Flex col wFull mt6 gap4 px4 py8 minHScreen mxAuto>
  <Card padding="lg" shadow="md">...</Card>
</Flex>
<RouteLink href="/" active>Login</RouteLink>

// ❌
<Flex className="mt-6 gap-4">
<RouteLink href="/" className="mb-nav-link-active" />
```

## Templates

- Prefer composing `@atoms` / `@molecules` with boolean props.
- Domain-specific layout wrappers belong in `templates` or `components`; extend atomic APIs instead of leaking `className`.
